WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.162 --> 00:00:06.333
- [Male] This guy's still
walking and following commands.

00:00:06.333 --> 00:00:08.434
- [Man] Time for taser, I think.

00:00:08.434 --> 00:00:11.016
- [Male] Gotta feeling
that's about to happen.

00:00:11.016 --> 00:00:12.515
- [Man] That looks like a bad dude, too.

00:00:12.515 --> 00:00:13.814
Could be on something.

00:00:13.814 --> 00:00:16.112
- [Man on Scanner] Which
way are they facing?

00:00:16.112 --> 00:00:18.042
- [Man] Police One,
they're facing westbound.

00:00:18.042 --> 00:00:20.343
I think he may have just been tasered.

00:00:20.343 --> 00:00:22.688
- [Female Officer] Shots fired!

00:00:22.688 --> 00:00:23.814
- [Male] Ooh!
- [Man] I have a 321.

00:00:23.814 --> 00:00:24.647
We have shots fired.

00:00:24.647 --> 00:00:26.184
We have one suspect down.

00:00:26.184 --> 00:00:28.311
We need insta here.

00:00:28.311 --> 00:00:31.028
- [Male] We need to get
this eastbound closed down

00:00:31.028 --> 00:00:31.975
if they could because they're not going

00:00:31.975 --> 00:00:33.251
to be able to let anybody...

00:00:33.251 --> 00:00:34.392
- [Male] Okay.

00:00:34.392 --> 00:00:37.642
(slow, dramatic music)

00:00:41.547 --> 00:00:43.564
- [Woman] There are
instances on battlefields

00:00:43.564 --> 00:00:45.454
of gruesome, gruesome wars where people

00:00:45.454 --> 00:00:47.481
have their hands up, and they live.

00:00:47.481 --> 00:00:49.087
And those are on battlefields,

00:00:49.087 --> 00:00:51.037
and we're talking about freeways.

00:00:51.037 --> 00:00:53.066
- I think now when I hear the word police,

00:00:53.066 --> 00:00:55.937
I feel very differently than
I did when I was younger.

00:00:55.937 --> 00:00:58.396
I think growing up,
clearly as a white woman,

00:00:58.396 --> 00:01:00.287
police was mostly a positive word to me.

00:01:00.287 --> 00:01:01.401
It was people who kept me safe.

00:01:01.401 --> 00:01:03.388
It was people who were in my family.

00:01:03.388 --> 00:01:05.171
I think as as someone who has never had

00:01:05.171 --> 00:01:06.989
any issues with the law,
it never occurred me

00:01:06.989 --> 00:01:10.018
that I'd have any sort of
negative interaction with police.

00:01:10.018 --> 00:01:12.610
So the word police, and
the concept growing up,

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:16.059
was a very positive, helpful
word that I felt fine about.

00:01:16.059 --> 00:01:19.462
As I've grown up, and as
I've become more aware of

00:01:19.462 --> 00:01:20.892
the climate that we're living in,

00:01:20.892 --> 00:01:22.375
the meaning and the tone of that word

00:01:22.375 --> 00:01:23.835
has changed completely.

00:01:23.835 --> 00:01:26.961
- Police are doing some
things that makes me feel

00:01:26.961 --> 00:01:28.923
that I don't know if they are

00:01:28.923 --> 00:01:30.425
who I would call for safety.

00:01:30.425 --> 00:01:31.591
- It's just upsetting that in a

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:35.320
law-enforcement profession,
having the wrong

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:38.024
intentions or thinking too
quickly about something

00:01:38.024 --> 00:01:40.941
could result in the loss of a life.

00:01:41.852 --> 00:01:45.389
- As a black man, the question has become,

00:01:45.389 --> 00:01:47.666
will the world allow me to live?

00:01:47.666 --> 00:01:50.249
- It's so unfortunate and so...

00:01:52.205 --> 00:01:53.706
sad to think that

00:01:53.706 --> 00:01:55.597
we live in the greatest
country in the world,

00:01:55.597 --> 00:01:59.180
and the people who are
here to protect that

00:02:00.159 --> 00:02:01.791
make us feel unprotected.

00:02:01.791 --> 00:02:03.314
- And it's interesting because it's like,

00:02:03.314 --> 00:02:07.533
I feel like every single time
a black person is killed,

00:02:07.533 --> 00:02:10.272
we always say, "This one is different."

00:02:10.272 --> 00:02:13.460
And it's not, because you
can have your hands up,

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:15.090
you can be reading a book in your car,

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:16.351
you can be disabled.

00:02:16.351 --> 00:02:17.984
You're just automatically a threat.

00:02:17.984 --> 00:02:19.035
It's not new.

00:02:19.035 --> 00:02:20.962
It's just we're being
killed in a different way.

00:02:20.962 --> 00:02:23.759
- Look at the last year. Maybe
one time it's an accident.

00:02:23.759 --> 00:02:26.479
Maybe one time it's an isolated incident.

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:28.239
And when it's this many times,

00:02:28.239 --> 00:02:31.458
like how many times have we
had to watch videos of this?

00:02:31.458 --> 00:02:32.915
- One of the first
things a cop should do is

00:02:32.915 --> 00:02:35.501
admit that we are all
born with a racial bias.

00:02:35.501 --> 00:02:40.255
- I think it is so built into
our society, and our culture,

00:02:40.255 --> 00:02:42.864
and our media, and the lessons
that we learn as children,

00:02:42.864 --> 00:02:44.342
that I think people reply on that.

00:02:44.342 --> 00:02:45.401
Then if you're a police officer,

00:02:45.401 --> 00:02:46.765
and you're trying to decide constantly

00:02:46.765 --> 00:02:48.944
who's good, who's bad,
who's a threat, who's not.

00:02:48.944 --> 00:02:50.120
But the second there's a doubt,

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:52.345
all of these subconscious
biases and opinions

00:02:52.345 --> 00:02:53.979
and beliefs that we've
been taught since childhood

00:02:53.979 --> 00:02:55.354
in this country come up.

00:02:55.354 --> 00:02:58.176
And they think, it seems likely
that person will have a gun.

00:02:58.176 --> 00:03:00.130
It seems likely that
person's going to hurt me.

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:01.954
I mean, you look from a helicopter,

00:03:01.954 --> 00:03:03.572
and you say, "That's one bad dude."

00:03:03.572 --> 00:03:04.405
How do you know?

00:03:04.405 --> 00:03:06.483
You only know because you've
been raised in this country

00:03:06.483 --> 00:03:09.155
where you are being
subconsciously told all the time

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:11.854
that guys who look like
that are bad dudes.

00:03:11.854 --> 00:03:13.633
- I definitely think that some people go

00:03:13.633 --> 00:03:15.861
into the police force with
the best of intentions,

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:19.026
and I know some people that
have and they're good people.

00:03:19.026 --> 00:03:23.546
But ultimately it's to
keep the system in place.

00:03:23.546 --> 00:03:26.916
And the system that currently
exists hurts minorities.

00:03:26.916 --> 00:03:28.509
It does not stand up for everyone.

00:03:28.509 --> 00:03:32.426
It is based purely on
inequality and injustice.

00:03:33.653 --> 00:03:36.022
It should be that we are all the same.

00:03:36.022 --> 00:03:37.587
That we are all brothers and sisters,

00:03:37.587 --> 00:03:40.254
but this world thinks otherwise.

00:03:41.381 --> 00:03:43.878
- I think we got here
because of 300 years,

00:03:43.878 --> 00:03:45.684
or more, of slavery.

00:03:45.684 --> 00:03:47.293
I think we got here because

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:50.140
the idea of black people being humans

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:51.735
is less than a century old.

00:03:51.735 --> 00:03:55.180
I think that we got here because

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:58.889
after MLK made the "I
Have A Dream" speech,

00:03:58.889 --> 00:04:01.262
people thought that it was
over, that it was done,

00:04:01.262 --> 00:04:03.385
that everything was finished,

00:04:03.385 --> 00:04:06.330
and I think we continue
to operate under the guise

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:08.778
that we live in a post-racial America,

00:04:08.778 --> 00:04:10.670
thus we stopped talking about race

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:12.072
and how we can progress it.

00:04:12.072 --> 00:04:14.224
- I am not hopeful at all.

00:04:14.224 --> 00:04:16.022
I've lost hope.

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:19.939
I don't think that anything
is going to change.

00:04:23.009 --> 00:04:24.426
And that's scary,

00:04:27.293 --> 00:04:29.626
because I want to have kids,

00:04:30.543 --> 00:04:32.047
and I want to have a husband.

00:04:32.047 --> 00:04:33.533
I want to have a life,

00:04:33.533 --> 00:04:35.593
and I want to live my
life unapologetically.

00:04:35.593 --> 00:04:37.665
I want my friends to be able

00:04:37.665 --> 00:04:39.248
to live their lives unapologetically,

00:04:39.248 --> 00:04:41.453
and I don't see that happening

00:04:41.453 --> 00:04:42.811
without always being fearful.

00:04:42.811 --> 00:04:46.472
Without always thinking twice
about everything that we do.

00:04:46.472 --> 00:04:50.329
I can't even drive down the
street without being like,

00:04:50.329 --> 00:04:51.763
"Are there any cops?

00:04:51.763 --> 00:04:52.596
"What's going to happen?"

00:04:52.596 --> 00:04:54.539
Or like having a cop car drive behind me.

00:04:54.539 --> 00:04:57.901
That is the scariest
thing for me right now,

00:04:57.901 --> 00:05:00.450
and I shouldn't have to be scared of that.

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:03.104
It's just a cop car behind me.

00:05:03.104 --> 00:05:04.176
That makes me scared.

00:05:04.176 --> 00:05:05.740
I don't have any hope right now.

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:08.261
- Even for myself, I have witnessed

00:05:08.261 --> 00:05:11.576
all these terrible things
that have been going on,

00:05:11.576 --> 00:05:13.015
just like everyone else,

00:05:13.015 --> 00:05:14.949
but with this last one

00:05:14.949 --> 00:05:16.486
it just felt a little different for me,

00:05:16.486 --> 00:05:19.196
and I know that everyone
needs to feel that

00:05:19.196 --> 00:05:21.223
because it's not okay.

00:05:21.223 --> 00:05:23.669
- I have 100% believed that this country

00:05:23.669 --> 00:05:27.022
is afraid of black men because
this country has been taught

00:05:27.022 --> 00:05:30.030
that black men are inherently monsters.

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:34.834
In every video we've seen
of these police shooting

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:36.254
these black men,

00:05:36.254 --> 00:05:38.880
if you look into that
police officer's eyes,

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:40.630
they are rarely calm.

00:05:41.657 --> 00:05:44.106
They're usually freaking out.

00:05:44.106 --> 00:05:47.459
They're usually heightened
beyond imagination.

00:05:47.459 --> 00:05:50.725
The video of Philando Castile
has the police officer

00:05:50.725 --> 00:05:54.009
shaking as hard as he can because he just

00:05:54.009 --> 00:05:57.592
has this idea that
Philando Castile is this

00:05:58.526 --> 00:06:02.906
inhuman monster that can jump
out at him or attack him.

00:06:02.906 --> 00:06:06.518
- The untrained, nervous
person has to be the most

00:06:06.518 --> 00:06:10.935
calm and collected human being
over the trained authority.

00:06:10.935 --> 00:06:13.434
- I think we need more social workers.

00:06:13.434 --> 00:06:15.064
I think we need more counselors.

00:06:15.064 --> 00:06:18.208
I think we need more community leaders.

00:06:18.208 --> 00:06:22.481
What I don't think we need
is police officers who

00:06:22.481 --> 00:06:24.683
are afraid of people.

00:06:24.683 --> 00:06:27.184
You can't be afraid of people

00:06:27.184 --> 00:06:29.461
when you have to go into
their communities everyday

00:06:29.461 --> 00:06:31.796
in their worst times.

00:06:31.796 --> 00:06:33.084
In their most troubling times,

00:06:33.084 --> 00:06:34.971
you have to see people, and

00:06:34.971 --> 00:06:36.464
if you're afraid of that,

00:06:36.464 --> 00:06:39.508
if you can't deal with that,

00:06:39.508 --> 00:06:42.159
I don't think police officers
should be a thing then.

00:06:42.159 --> 00:06:45.238
- I feel like you grow up now,
in school you watch videos of

00:06:45.238 --> 00:06:47.725
MLK, and the marches, and
the civil rights movement,

00:06:47.725 --> 00:06:49.076
and everyone goes, "Oh, I totally

00:06:49.076 --> 00:06:50.186
"would have been a part of that."

00:06:50.186 --> 00:06:52.031
But, what they don't realize is,

00:06:52.031 --> 00:06:53.297
that is what's happening now.

00:06:53.297 --> 00:06:54.606
This is the time.

00:06:54.606 --> 00:06:56.122
This is not something that we can

00:06:56.122 --> 00:06:59.694
drown ourselves out with news
of Brangelina breaking up,

00:06:59.694 --> 00:07:03.585
or whatever Kylie Jenner's
latest lip gear is.

00:07:03.585 --> 00:07:06.849
This is the moment, and this is the time.

00:07:06.849 --> 00:07:08.451
We have to change this,

00:07:08.451 --> 00:07:10.496
and no one else is gonna change this,

00:07:10.496 --> 00:07:13.150
and honestly, to other white people,

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:14.894
this cannot change without us.

00:07:14.894 --> 00:07:16.131
That's just how this works,

00:07:16.131 --> 00:07:20.492
because we are still most of
the power in this country,

00:07:20.492 --> 00:07:22.568
and it has to also come from above.

00:07:22.568 --> 00:07:25.005
It has to come from the
streets and from social media,

00:07:25.005 --> 00:07:27.526
but it also has to come from above,

00:07:27.526 --> 00:07:28.619
from positions of power

00:07:28.619 --> 00:07:30.112
from people who can
actually make a change,

00:07:30.112 --> 00:07:34.723
from people who can add policies
into police enforcement,

00:07:34.723 --> 00:07:36.697
who can change whether
people wear bodycams,

00:07:36.697 --> 00:07:39.675
who can change whether
these police officers

00:07:39.675 --> 00:07:42.011
are prosecuted when they kill someone

00:07:42.011 --> 00:07:43.412
who has no right to be killed.

00:07:43.412 --> 00:07:45.934
Every time that happens, we
take a million steps back.

00:07:45.934 --> 00:07:46.967
There are people, there are judges,

00:07:46.967 --> 00:07:48.744
there are lawyers, there are jurors,

00:07:48.744 --> 00:07:50.473
there are people in that courtroom

00:07:50.473 --> 00:07:52.047
who could make a
difference, who could say,

00:07:52.047 --> 00:07:53.597
"This is unacceptable, and this is

00:07:53.597 --> 00:07:55.399
"a sign that it's unacceptable."

00:07:55.399 --> 00:07:58.421
But when those people,
many of whom are white,

00:07:58.421 --> 00:07:59.485
do not stand up for this,

00:07:59.485 --> 00:08:01.619
and do not do what's right,

00:08:01.619 --> 00:08:03.374
it just shows all the
other police officers,

00:08:03.374 --> 00:08:05.303
all the other people who are
considering being violent

00:08:05.303 --> 00:08:06.276
towards other people,

00:08:06.276 --> 00:08:07.266
that they're not going to be punished.

00:08:07.266 --> 00:08:08.811
That it's not something we value.

00:08:08.811 --> 00:08:11.390
- Ultimately, it comes
down to people power.

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:14.243
If enough good people
stand up in solidarity

00:08:14.243 --> 00:08:16.220
and fight the good fight,

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:18.446
which means bringing about justice,

00:08:18.446 --> 00:08:20.113
then we can create a community

00:08:20.113 --> 00:08:22.224
where we are all protecting each other.

00:08:22.224 --> 00:08:25.391
(gentle guitar music)

00:08:26.424 --> 00:08:28.126
- I understand all the
pressure that you feel

00:08:28.126 --> 00:08:31.347
to not say anything and
to support where you work,

00:08:31.347 --> 00:08:32.860
but this isn't what you signed up for.

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:35.845
This isn't what you took your oath for.

00:08:35.845 --> 00:08:39.512
- I would say to the
police that I love you,

00:08:40.731 --> 00:08:45.379
and I respect the sacrifice
that you make everyday

00:08:45.379 --> 00:08:48.712
to put your life on the line for others.

00:08:49.629 --> 00:08:53.160
But what I am asking
for you is to understand

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:55.514
that because of the way things are,

00:08:55.514 --> 00:08:58.681
my mother is making the same sacrifice

00:08:59.669 --> 00:09:01.227
that your mother makes,

00:09:01.227 --> 00:09:03.591
knowing that every day
you go out on the street,

00:09:03.591 --> 00:09:06.794
you have the possibility
of getting killed.

00:09:06.794 --> 00:09:09.298
I'll stop being afraid of you

00:09:09.298 --> 00:09:12.216
when you're willing to
stop being afraid of me.

00:09:12.216 --> 00:09:13.153
- Everybody wants to get home.

00:09:13.153 --> 00:09:14.616
No one wants to die.

00:09:14.616 --> 00:09:17.645
Try to keep in mind, like if
you were to reverse the roles

00:09:17.645 --> 00:09:19.575
and someone pulled up on you with a gun,

00:09:19.575 --> 00:09:20.592
how are you going to feel?

00:09:20.592 --> 00:09:22.009
Let's try to make sure everybody

00:09:22.009 --> 00:09:24.183
can get to see the next day.

00:09:24.183 --> 00:09:27.183
(soft, quiet music)

00:09:28.594 --> 00:09:30.594
- It's not going unheard

00:09:32.194 --> 00:09:34.729
and unwatched and unlistened to,

00:09:34.729 --> 00:09:39.353
and it's such an awful
sacrifice to have to sacrifice

00:09:39.353 --> 00:09:42.055
a loved one to make people care,

00:09:42.055 --> 00:09:43.469
and to make people wake up,

00:09:43.469 --> 00:09:46.332
and to make people do better
and fight for what is right.

00:09:46.332 --> 00:09:48.675
But please know that not only

00:09:48.675 --> 00:09:52.479
are your family members'
names going to be heard,

00:09:52.479 --> 00:09:54.818
but this is what's going to change it.

00:09:54.818 --> 00:09:58.336
- I would say to them that I do not take

00:09:58.336 --> 00:09:59.840
your son's sacrifice lightly.

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:01.956
I do not take your
daughter's sacrifice lightly.

00:10:01.956 --> 00:10:04.252
I do not take your
father's sacrifice lightly,

00:10:04.252 --> 00:10:07.651
or your mother's sacrifice
lightly, and that

00:10:07.651 --> 00:10:12.050
I will continue to do all
that I can to make sure that

00:10:12.050 --> 00:10:13.857
people do not forget their names,

00:10:13.857 --> 00:10:18.168
and do not forget the
importance of their sacrifice.

00:10:18.168 --> 00:10:21.037
- (sniffs) We will never
understand your pain.

00:10:21.037 --> 00:10:22.370
We won't, but...

00:10:25.583 --> 00:10:27.808
I promise that I will life a life

00:10:27.808 --> 00:10:29.870
charged with making change.

00:10:29.870 --> 00:10:32.444
- I'm sorry that this happened to you,

00:10:32.444 --> 00:10:35.561
and I'm standing here with you,

00:10:35.561 --> 00:10:37.087
because the only way

00:10:37.087 --> 00:10:39.341
that this terrible wrong could be righted

00:10:39.341 --> 00:10:43.258
is if we stop it from
happening to anyone else.

00:10:44.445 --> 00:10:47.195
- I would say you deserve better.

00:10:48.852 --> 00:10:50.341
You deserved better.

00:10:50.341 --> 00:10:52.674
Your family deserved better.

00:10:56.244 --> 00:10:58.161
I would say I love you,

00:10:59.552 --> 00:11:01.635
and I care, and I'm here.

00:11:02.951 --> 00:11:04.784
And as tired and angry

00:11:08.246 --> 00:11:10.079
as I am, I will fight.

00:11:12.624 --> 00:11:16.707
I will fight to honor the
lives as best as I can,

00:11:18.119 --> 00:11:22.034
because it is not your job alone to do so,

00:11:22.034 --> 00:11:24.774
and we can't do it alone.

00:11:24.774 --> 00:11:27.191
(soft music)

